.Dd October 5, 2026
.Dt AIRPLANE-MODE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm airplane-mode
.Nd turn airplane mode on or off
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm Cm on
.Nm Cm off
.Nm Cm toggle
.Nm Cm status
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
asks
.Xr airplane-radiosd 8
to turn the WLAN interface and Bluetooth off
.Pq Cm on
or back on
.Pq Cm off ,
then shows
.Cm airplane-on
or
.Cm airplane-off
through
.Xr bosd 1
for 2 seconds.
.Cm toggle
flips the intended state.
.Cm status
prints
.Cm on
or
.Cm off
and does not show a glyph.
.Pp
The intended state is written to
.Pa ~/.cache/airplane-mode.state
before the radios move.
A press while the glyph is still up still toggles, and the daemon
is asked to catch up to the latest
.Cm on
or
.Cm off .
.Pp
The socket is
.Ev airplane_radiosd_socket ,
or
.Pa /var/run/airplane-radiosd.sock
when that is unset.
If the socket is missing,
.Nm
reports that and does not change the radios.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "airplane_radiosd_socket"
.It Ev airplane_radiosd_socket
Control socket.
The default is
.Pa /var/run/airplane-radiosd.sock .
.It Ev DISPLAY
X server for
.Nm bosd .
The default is
.Pa :0 .
.It Ev HOME
Directory above
.Pa .cache/airplane-mode.state .
When unset, the state file is under
.Pa /tmp .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.cache/airplane-mode.state"
.It Pa ~/.cache/airplane-mode.state
Intended airplane state,
.Cm on
or
.Cm off .
.It Pa /tmp/airplane-mode.state.lock
Lock around the state flip.
.It Pa /tmp/airplane-mode.apply.lock
Lock around the request to the daemon.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Cm on ,
.Cm off ,
and
.Cm toggle
exit 0 once the request is queued.
.Cm status
exits 0 when the daemon replies
.Cm on
or
.Cm off ,
and 1 otherwise.
A bad argument exits 64.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr airplane-mode-toggle 1 ,
.Xr bhotkeys 1 ,
.Xr bosd 1 ,
.Xr airplane-radiosd 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
